From fe53eb4bd7fdfa6e1d76eb669f12130f6df3decc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:26:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Avoid hosts for unplaced child swapchains

Battle.net's login tree wraps the real swap-chain content in a first-level
child visual with identity placement, no clip, and no transform. Hosting that
visual in a Win32 child HWND is not useful, and on native Wayland the child
HWND is not a managed surface. DXVK can present to it successfully while KWin
and the user still see the black parent window.

Keep child host HWNDs for actual placed, clipped, surface-backed, or nested
composition layers, but bind unplaced first-level swap-chain wrappers directly
to the DComp target HWND.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <Alexander.Schiffhauer@gmail.com>
---
 dlls/dcomp/device.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/device.c b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
index c8f2deb..ba0980d 100644
--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -1268,7 +1268,7 @@ static BOOL dcomp_visual_needs_host(const struct dcomp_visual *v, BOOL has_surfa
              v->transform.m11 != 1.0f || v->transform.m22 != 1.0f;
     if (placed) return TRUE;
 
-    if (v->parent) return TRUE;
+    if (v->parent && v->parent->parent) return TRUE;
 
     return FALSE;
 }
